cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "airgap: running Qwen3.8-27B offline on Apple Silicon as a local Claude Code backend"
message: "If you use this project, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bova
    given-names: Simone
    affiliation: Yempik
  - name: Yempik
    alias: yempik-ai
repository-code: "https://github.com/yempik-ai/airgap"
url: "https://github.com/yempik-ai/airgap"
abstract: >-
  An open-source guide and script kit for running the Qwen3.8-27B language model
  entirely offline on an Apple Silicon Mac in MLX format, and using it as the local
  backend for Claude Code in place of the Anthropic API. Supports the uncensored
  (abliterated, decensored, refusal-removed) build of Qwen3.8-27B as well as the
  stock builds, at 4-bit, 5-bit and 8-bit quantization. The scripts detect the host
  Mac's unified memory and derive their own context window, memory floor and cache
  budgets; they refuse to start rather than let the machine swap, and refuse any
  configuration that would expose the model beyond loopback. Documentation covers
  hardware requirements, installation for readers with no terminal experience,
  memory safety on Apple's unified-memory architecture, troubleshooting, and a
  first-principles explanation of quantization, KV caching, hybrid linear attention
  and speculative decoding. No model weights are distributed.
keywords:
  - qwen
  - qwen3.8
  - mlx
  - apple-silicon
  - claude-code
  - local-llm
  - offline-llm
  - uncensored
  - abliterated
